Thank you for looking at it. "QCA9377" is the module's name (IMC
Networks), as in dc16388d45ec and in the earlier 04ca:3015 and
0cf3:e500 entries. This is what the controller itself reports to
btusb_setup_qca(), with the files from linux-firmware:

  QCA_GET_TARGET_VERSION: rom_version 0x00000302, patch 0x111
  status 0x20, so both files are loaded:
    qca/rampatch_usb_00000302.bin  returns 0
    qca/nvm_usb_00000302.bin       returns 0
  version read afterwards: patch 0x3e8

0x00000302 is the "Rome 3.2" entry of qca_devices_table. So, if I
read you right, the Bluetooth part of this module is a Rome 3.2
(QCA6174A) core, and QCA9377 is only the module's name?

If so, question 1 stands for Rome 3.2 on its ROM firmware. If not,
which setup should this device get instead?

